            {
              "id": "a9b6f6d0-e09a-4560-a72d-ae3d189958ca",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Universe in a Handkerchief: Lewis Carroll’s Mathematical Recreations, Games, Puzzles, &amp; Word Plays </strong></em>was written by Martin Gardner, originally published by Copernicus in 1996."
            },
            {
              "id": "169386e5-15b2-4840-b4bd-8ac0373b0b71",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "595e389b-a34d-47d6-9d51-905d21088e64",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>This book contains scores of intriguing puzzles and paradoxes from Lewis Carroll, the author of </em>Alice in Wonderland<em>, whose interests ranged from inventing new games like Arithmetical Croquet to important problems in symbolic logic and propositional calculus. Written by Carroll expert and well-known mathematics author Martin Gardner, this tour through Carroll's inventions is both fun and informative.</em>"
            }
          ]
